	(text_box "Concept:\nThis Board uses an GateMate FPGA\nin combination with an USB PHY\nand ab ISO 7816 Interface to\nsimulate an\n  \nToDo Next Revision:\n- Combine the two USB-C 5V LEDs into one \n- BOM verkleinern, v.a. Kondensatoren\n- Power IC mit mehreren Buck convertern\n- PR2040 Flash did not work, replacement from Winbond did work\nDone:\n- Fixed 5V Diode\n- Power supply structure reworken\n- removed reset, header, 1nF caps\n- replaced power sturcture\n  -> buck for VDD_CORE\n  -> adj Buck for IO voltages\n  -> LDO for fixed 2V5 things: VDD_CLK, RAM\n  -> LDO for fixed 1V8 things: SRAM\n  -> LDO for fixed 3V3 things: RP2040USB\n- Upgraded Interface to not reqire soldering to switch from master to slave and using a more common swich\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 12.7 0)
		(size 60.96 93.98)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
			(color 0 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "86d65f26-502f-4f5d-a125-b71988cc33ca")
	)
	(text_box "Notes:\n- Supports 3 classes: A,B,C\n- Different Supply Voltages: 5V, 3.3V, 1.8V\n- three AS - Application Specific pins\n- does not support +21V DC [Programming]\nIf used as Master:\n- Place all components\n- 5V direct pass though of the USB Voltage\n- 3.3V, 1.8V 500mA current limited"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 115.57 0)
		(size 55.88 26.67)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
